Title: The Hidden Self
Order: 1
Production Code: 1x01

INT. REUEL'S ROOM - EVENING

AMB: sleet against the window, a cylinder stove ticking as it cools

[[Reuel Briggs]], threadbare coat, sits alone among his books. A storm batters the glass. He reads from a battered volume on trance-states and the occult, then throws it down and starts pacing.

REUEL BRIGGS
(to himself)
I have the power. I know it's true. If I could only complete the experiments, I'd astonish the world.

He drops into his chair by the stove, back half-turned to the window. His gaze drifts out into the storm — and the darkness softens into cream and rose. A face resolves out of the weather: a woman's, fair-haired, eyes deep and earnest.

He reaches toward it. It fades.

REUEL BRIGGS (CONT'D)
(shaken)
The effect of the imagination. Nothing more.

SFX: a sharp knock, then a second, rat-tat

AUBREY LIVINGSTON (O.S.)
Open up, you inhospitable Turk! I know you're in there!

Reuel opens the door. [[Aubrey Livingston]] sweeps in, dripping, effortlessly at ease in a room that clearly isn't his.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Beastly night. What are you moping about in the dark for?

REUEL BRIGGS
The usual. Whence and whither.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
You ought to be renamed the Science of Trance-States. Come to a concert with me tonight instead of grinding yourself into the floor.

REUEL BRIGGS
Whose concert?

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
A jubilee troupe, up from the South. Tremont Temple. I have the tickets.

Reuel hesitates, still faintly unsettled by what he just saw in the glass.

REUEL BRIGGS
Well — if you say so.

They smoke in silence a moment, the storm still working at the window.
